model:aspect_precondition_eead0611_27d2_40ed_a2f3_bd7ab7cccd02 a fram:PreconditionAspect ;
    fram:aspectType "Precondition" ;
    fram:aspectCode "P" ;
    fram:semanticRole "Conditions that must exist before the function can execute" ;
    rdfs:comment "Precondition (P) represents the conditions that must be verified \nto exist before a function can be carried out. Preconditions are system conditions \nthat must be fulfilled, rather than things that are used or consumed.\nExamples: Access rights verified, safety checks completed, equipment ready, \nenvironmental conditions met." ;
    fram:analysisQuestions "What conditions must be true before this function can start?" ;
    fram:analysisQuestions "What must be verified before execution?" ;
    fram:analysisQuestions "What system states are prerequisites?" .

model:aspect_resource_eead0611_27d2_40ed_a2f3_bd7ab7cccd02 a fram:ResourceAspect ;
    fram:aspectType "Resource" ;
    fram:aspectCode "R" ;
    fram:semanticRole "What the function needs or consumes during execution" ;
    rdfs:comment "Resource (R) is what the function needs when it is carried out \nor what it consumes to produce the Output. Unlike Preconditions, Resources are \ntypically used up or occupied during function execution.\nExamples: Tools, equipment, energy, money, manpower, software, time allocation." ;
    fram:analysisQuestions "What does this function consume?" ;
    fram:analysisQuestions "What resources are needed for execution?" ;
    fram:analysisQuestions "What is used up or occupied during this function?" .

model:aspect_control_eead0611_27d2_40ed_a2f3_bd7ab7cccd02 a fram:ControlAspect ;
    fram:aspectType "Control" ;
    fram:aspectCode "C" ;
    fram:semanticRole "How the function is monitored, supervised, or regulated" ;
    rdfs:comment "Control (C) is how the function is monitored, supervised, or \nregulated so that it can adjust to produce the required Output. Control represents \nthe regulation or governance of the function.\nExamples: Procedures, guidelines, supervisory oversight, feedback loops, \nmonitoring systems, regulations." ;
    fram:analysisQuestions "How is this function monitored?" ;
    fram:analysisQuestions "What procedures or guidelines govern this function?" ;
    fram:analysisQuestions "How is the function adjusted during execution?" .

